@@ -0,0 +1,38 @@
+# Unwired H.264 reconstruction experiment
+
+This directory is a standalone lab, not an application decoder. Do not add it
+to the production project until the root GPU milestone gates are complete.
+The shader source is new experimental implementation, with the pinned LGPL
+FFmpeg kernels used as a separate test oracle. Generated oracle files preserve
+upstream notices and record source hashes; they are not shipped in the patch.
+
+From the repository root on Windows:
+
+```
+experiments\h264_gpu\build_host.cmd C:\absolute\path\to\opennow
+powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File experiments/h264_gpu/build_shaders.ps1
+```
+
+The first command needs Visual Studio C++ Build Tools, Windows SDK, Python,
+and D3D11 WARP. It executes shaders and compares exact output pixels with the
+pinned FFmpeg luma/IDCT oracle and an independent scalar chroma/weight oracle.
+The second uses the installed Xbox 360 SDK compiler. Neither runs on Xbox.
+
+Implemented kernels: all 16 luma qpel positions including unclipped diagonal
+intermediates; all 64 chroma fractional positions; unweighted, uniweighted,
+biweighted and averaged predictions; residual addition; FFmpeg-layout 4x4 and
+8x8 inverse transforms. Two-pass transforms preserve signed int16 intermediates
+in R32F resources, with explicit floor/round/clip operations.
+
+Resource contract: R32F reference planes contain exact byte values 0..255,
+R32F residual/coefficients contain signed integers, point sampling only, no
+sRGB, no blending, no MSAA. `dimensions` and `motion` are plane-specific;
+chroma motion values are eighth-pixel units. Coefficients are already inverse
+quantized and include FFmpeg's DC processing. 8x8 transforms need 8-aligned
+plane extents. Interpolation clamping uses coded picture borders, not display
+crop borders. The driver must validate every job before submission.
+
+Not implemented here: bitstream extraction, intra reconstruction, in-loop
+deblocking, DPB management, frame-thread integration or automatic CPU fallback.
+R32F is a correctness prototype, not a bandwidth-optimized production format.
+No throughput claim follows from shader compiler timing estimates.
